WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W7 (0.1.1)


STATE

  Version 0.1.1, Phase P2 (process control, traps, and special builtins),
  on branch dev. It adds:
  - background commands (&) parsed into TC_NODE_BG (in lists, compound
    lists, and function AST clones), executed with /dev/null stdin and
    ignored SIGINT/SIGQUIT when job control is off, setting $!;
  - background process tracking (src/bg.c) with non-blocking zombie
    reaping and the wait builtin (all jobs, specific PIDs, 127 for
    unknown/re-waited PIDs, EINTR interruption for trapped signals);
  - async-signal-safe signal flag dispatch (src/signals.c) and per-shell
    trap table (src/trap.c) supporting signals and EXIT at safe points
    only, inherited-SIG_IGN protection in non-interactive shells, and
    $(trap) subshell display preservation;
  - remaining POSIX special builtins (src/builtins_special.c): set
    (variables, positional params, -a/-f, -o/+o, refusing 0.1.3 options),
    shift, eval, . (dot, with PATH search, fd >= 10, and return),
    export, readonly, unset (-v/-f), exec (persistent redirections and
    process replacement), and times.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; FUNCNEST sets the function recursion limit; signed
  64-bit arithmetic overflow is a reported error.


